  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is replaced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Pt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> in the complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><msub><mi>NiCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>, which of the following properties are expected to get changed?<br />A. Geometry<br />B. Geometrical isomerism<br />C. Optical isomerism<br />D. Magnetic properties",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HwVow",
      "text": "A and D",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vwZO4",
      "text": "A, B and C",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FjE8w",
      "text": "B and C",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Dqx1k",
      "text": "A, B and D",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is replaced by<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Pt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> in the complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>NiCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>, the following properties are expected to be changed:</p><p>A. Geometry:&nbsp;Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Pt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> have different coordination preferences and atomic sizes, the replacement is likely to result in a change in the geometry of the complex. That is it changes to square planar.</p><p>B. Geometrical isomerism:&nbsp;If the replacement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Pt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> leads to a change in the ligand arrangement, it can result in the generation of cis and trans isomers.</p><p>C. Magnetic properties:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is diamagnetic.</p><p>Both the complex species are optically inactive.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
